;; The pinned corpus: real apps at fixed commits, each with the config
;; meta-source reads it with. `bb corpus fetch` clones them under
;; .corpus/apps/<repo>; `bb corpus run` checks each one. See corpus/README.md.
;;
;;   :id      the app's name in findings and labels
;;   :git     where it comes from, :sha the commit (never a branch)
;;   :path    instead of :git, a directory in this repository
;;   :root    the directory inside the checkout meta-source reads from
;;   :config  what meta-source.edn would say: :src, :registry, :packs.
;;            Opt-in checks are on (:report-unused): the corpus measures
;;            every check, not only the default ones
;;            (without it, the app's own meta-source.edn)
;;   :plants-only  only a place to plant defects: `run` skips it

